{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clutching clutching","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","fileName":"Clutching.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clutching","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D User Interface","Object Positioning","Object Rotation","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clutching clutching","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","fileName":"Clutching.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clutching","heading":"Clutching","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Clutching occurs when a manipulation cannot be completed in one motion, forcing the user to release, reposition, and reengage the control before continuing.\n\nA wrench used in a confined space is a physical example. In a [[3D User Interface]], limited device range or an unsuitable control mapping can produce the same repeated interruption during [[Object Positioning]] or [[Object Rotation]].\n\nClutching is wasted motion that can reduce performance and comfort. A precision grip, motion amplification, or a mapping with a more suitable range can reduce the number of regrasping cycles, though amplification can also reduce fine control.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D User Interface","Object Positioning","Object Rotation","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"clutching clutching","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Clutching.md","fileName":"Clutching.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Clutching","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Interaction","3D User Interface","Object Positioning","Object Rotation","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}